# MAD vLLM patch for docker/vllm_disagg_inference.glmv5.3_quark_mxfp4_attnfp8.ubuntu.amd.Dockerfile
# What: MoRI EPv1 prepare() slices the dispatch outputs to a host-side receive-row
#   bound (the bound EPv2 already uses), on the IntraNode kernel only. AITER then
#   sees M = world x padded batch instead of world x max_num_batched_tokens.
#   Must be run with VLLM_MORI_RECV_ROW_ALIGN=4096 (added by 0006): with the
#   default 32-row alignment the small-M AITER fused quant+sort path faulted on
#   DEP8 P/D. 4096 is a configuration workaround, not a root-cause fix.
# Upstream: local, not upstream. Overlaps vllm-project/vllm#63412 (open; same slice,
#   different bound, not gated to IntraNode).
#   https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/63412
# Remove when: #63412 (or an equivalent bound) is merged and VLLM_REF contains it,
#   and the AITER small-M fault is fixed or ruled out at the default alignment.
# Note: the commit-message preamble below was reworded for publication; the diff
#   hunks are byte-identical to the tested patch (tested file sha256 df6384b3...).
# ---- end of MAD header; the patch follows (diff hunks as tested) ----
From 8a72cd321bb5f874ae8c0d28d4c3c15461d4cad2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shiksha Patel <shiksha.patel@amd.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 04:59:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [ROCm][Perf][MoE] MoRI EPv1: bound IntraNode receive rows by
 DP token counts

MoriPrepareAndFinalize.prepare() returns MoRI's receive buffers unchanged.
They hold max_num_tokens_to_recv() = world_size * max_num_tokens rows, and
the modular kernel takes the expert M from them, so AITER fused_moe looks up
its tuned config and sizes its sorted buffers and GEMM grids from
world_size * max_num_batched_tokens rows on every decode step. Only the
first expert_num_tokens rows are real; AITER already limits sorting to them
via num_local_tokens, but not the config lookup or the grid.

EPv2 already slices its receive buffers to a host-side bound derived from
DPMetadata.num_tokens_across_dp_cpu (#61361). Move that bound to a module
function and apply it in EPv1 as well. Only for the IntraNode kernel,
which packs received rows into [0, total_recv); InterNode keeps the full
buffer. The bound needs no device sync, and under CUDA graphs all DP ranks
are padded to the captured size, so it is fixed per graph.

Local patch, not upstream. Overlaps the open
vllm#63412 (same EPv1 slice with a different bound, InterNode included).
Base: 8673602b8b + patches 0001-0003; also applies to cd1effa2e7.
